From: zenlte local fix (v3)
Subject: [PATCH] recovery: stop requesting extra_attr/project_quota when formatting f2fs

Apply in: src/bootable/recovery

Same bug as patch 0003, in the LineageOS recovery's own format_volume():
"-O project_quota,extra_attr" was hardcoded.  Keeping recovery and fs_mgr in
agreement matters -- otherwise recovery would format a filesystem the booted
ROM cannot survive, which is precisely the class of mismatch that produced the
original panic.

diff --git a/recovery_utils/roots.cpp b/recovery_utils/roots.cpp
index fc69df83..f97e5852 100644
--- a/recovery_utils/roots.cpp
+++ b/recovery_utils/roots.cpp
@@ -334,8 +334,12 @@ int format_volume(const std::string& volume, const std::string& directory,
     "android",
   };
 
-  make_f2fs_cmd.push_back("-O");
-  make_f2fs_cmd.push_back("project_quota,extra_attr");
+  // zenlte (Exynos7420) local change -- DEVICE SPECIFIC.
+  // Do not request extra_attr/project_quota: this device's 3.10 kernel has no
+  // i_extra_isize in struct f2fs_inode, so an extra_attr filesystem makes it
+  // read inode metadata as block addresses and panic in update_sit_entry().
+  // Keeping recovery and fs_mgr in agreement matters -- otherwise recovery
+  // would format a filesystem the booted ROM cannot survive.
 
   if (needs_casefold) {
     make_f2fs_cmd.push_back("-O");
